   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Days, time and inversion",
     "texto": [
      "The days of the week in Dutch are: maandag (Monday), dinsdag (Tuesday), woensdag (Wednesday), donderdag (Thursday), vrijdag (Friday), zaterdag (Saturday), zondag (Sunday). To ask the time: «Hoe laat is het?» (What time is it?), and to answer: «Het is acht uur» (It is eight o'clock). Golden rule of inversion! If you start the sentence with a time expression such as «Vandaag», the verb must go in 2nd position and the subject moves to 3rd position: «Vandaag is het maandag» (and never *Vandaag het is...). Unlike English, which keeps the subject first («Today it is Monday»), Dutch switches the verb and the subject."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
